SUMMARY:[Robustness & Safety][Privacy-preserving ML] SaTML 2027 - Mandatory
  abstract registration deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: IEEE Conference on Secure and Trustworthy Mac
 hine Learning\nWebsite: https://satml.org/\nSource URL: https://satml.org
 /call-for-papers/\nLocation: Reykjavik\, Iceland\nTopics: Robustness & Sa
 fety\, Privacy-preserving ML\, Fairness & Responsible AI\, Explainability
  & Interpretability\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based / systematizat
 ion of knowledge / position papers\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked d
 ate: 2026-10-07\nNotes: Fifth annual edition. Main meeting May 4-6\; work
 shops May 3. The mandatory registration and new-paper deadlines have pass
 ed. Revisions are restricted to existing submissions and do not reopen ne
 w-paper opportunities. Camera-ready is only announced as mid-February\, e
 xact date TBC\, so no exact camera-ready event is invented. Size M is an 
 editorial estimate.\nScope: Security\, safety\, and trustworthiness of ma
 chine learning. Characteristic work studies attacks and defenses\, privac
 y\, verification\, ML-system security\, fairness\, interpretability\, and
  trustworthy data curation. Theoretical\, empirical\, and applied papers 
 must engage substantively with a safety or trustworthiness question\; mer
 ely using an ML model is insufficient.\nAdditional topics: Machine Learni
 ng\, ML Systems & Infrastructure\nScope sources (2027): https://satml.org
 /call-for-papers/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://satml.org/call-for-papers/
